      "text": "Given that the set of three numbers has both a mean and median equal to 4, and the smallest number is 1, let's denote the three numbers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) where \\(a \\leq b \\leq c\\).\n\nSince the mean of the numbers is 4, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b + c}{3} = 4\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we get:\n\\[\na + b + c = 12\n\\]\nWe are also given that the median of the set is 4. Since the median is the middle number, we have:\n\\[\nb = 4\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(b = 4\\) into the equation \\(a + b + c = 12\\), we get:\n\\[\na + 4 + c = 12\n\\]\nSimplifying this, we find:\n\\[\na + c = 8\n\\]\nWe need to determine the range of the set, which is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers, \\(c - a\\). To find \\(c\\), we express it in terms of \\(a\\) using the equation \\(a + c = 8\\):\n\\[\nc = 8 - a\n\\]\nSince \\(a \\leq b \\leq c\\) and \\(b = 4\\), it follows that \\(a \\leq 4 \\leq 8 - a\\). This gives us the inequality:\n\\[\na \\leq 4\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n8 - a \\geq 4 \\implies a \\leq 4\n\\]\nThe inequality \\(a \\leq 4\\) is already satisfied by the condition \\(a \\leq 4\\). To find the range, we need to determine the maximum and minimum values of \\(c\\). The value of \\(c\\) will be maximized when \\(a\\) is minimized, and minimized when \\(a\\) is maximized. However, since \\(a\\) and \\(c\\) are symmetric and must sum to 8, the most straightforward and logical conclusion is that \\(a\\) can be any value less than or equal to 4, and \\(c\\) will be the corresponding value to keep the sum 8. \n\nThe range is:\n\\[\nc - a = (8 - a) - a = 8 - 2a\n\\]\nSince \\(a\\) can be any value less than or equal to 4, the maximum value of \\(8 - 2a\\) occurs when \\(a\\) is minimized (i.e., \\(a = 4\\)):\n\\[\nc - a = 8 - 2(4) = 8 - 8 = 0\n\\]\nHowever, since \\(a = 4\\) would make \\(c = 4\\) (which is not possible because \\(a \\leq 4\\) and \\(a < 4\\)), the maximum value is approached but not achieved in this set of constraints. The actual minimum value of \\(c - a\\) occurs when \\(a\\) is maximized (i.e., very close to 4 but less than 4):\n\\[\nc - a \\approx 8 - 2 \\times \\text{(some value close to 4, but not 4)}\n\\]\nSince the problem asks for the range and we have the constraints, the most logical and practical range based on the given constraints is the difference between the maximum and minimum values of \\(c - a\\) within the valid range of \\(a\\), which is from slightly less than 4 to 0. However, the practical and smallest feasible range based on the constraints is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
